-- Tuffy Flow: club seed data
--
-- Source: two sources, joined.
--   1. Student Life and Leadership's registered organization list, 22 September
--      2026, obtained as a CSV. 320 orgs, every one FULLY RE-REGISTERED. This
--      is the roster: it decides which orgs belong in the app.
--      https://www.fullerton.edu/sll/involvement/clubs/
--   2. TitanLink, CSUF's student organization directory, read 1 October 2026
--      from /engage/api/discovery/search/organizations?top=1000
--      701 records, 391 of them Active. This supplies the id, the summary, the
--      description, the website key and the categories.
--      https://fullerton.campuslabs.com/engage
--
--   All 320 roster names resolve to a TitanLink record. Three are written
--   differently by the two systems and had to be matched by hand:
--     Pickleball Club            -> Pickleball (383202)
--     Society of Automotive Eng. -> Society of Automotive Engineering - Formula (137052)
--     CSUF Ski and Snowboard Club -> Ski and Snowboard Club (383119)
--   That last one matters more than it looks: seed_events.sql joins clubs by
--   name, so dropping the CSUF prefix is load bearing.
--
--   Moving Forward Community @ CSUF (423736) is a separate case. It is on the
--   roster but TitanLink has frozen it since. It is kept, with its real status
--   in the status column, because the roster says who is registered.
--
--   An earlier version of this file carried 66 of them, filtered on TitanLink's
--   Status alone. Active only means the page is live, not that the org is
--   registered this year, which is why the roster decides and not the directory.
--   Nothing in the app fetches TitanLink at runtime.
--
-- categories  TitanLink's CategoryNames, verbatim. Theirs.
-- tags        our own matching vocabulary. Ours, not a TitanLink field.
--             Keyword matched against the name and the summary, plus a mapping
--             from the topical categories.
--             Category names are deliberately kept out of the keyword text:
--             "College of Engineering and Computer Science" sits on orgs that
--             have nothing to do with either, and matching on it tagged a
--             Bhangra dance team as a software club.
--             Where an org has ticked more than eight categories its list says
--             nothing, so only its own words are used.
--             Keywords are anchored to word boundaries, because the loose
--             version read "venture" out of Adventure Club, "rowing" out of
--             "growing in love for God", and "arts" out of "martial arts".
--             The word "programming" is deliberately not a keyword: in student
--             org writing it usually means events, not code, which is why Titan
--             TV does not come back as a software club.
-- Summaries and descriptions are TitanLink's with HTML and URLs stripped, so
-- not byte for byte theirs.

-- Re-runnable: the real TitanLink rows are the only clubs that should exist.
delete from clubs;

on conflict (titanlink_id) do nothing;

-- Assert the roster loaded in full. A short load would otherwise look like a
-- small campus rather than a broken seed. A club being renamed is caught
-- separately, by the event count check at the end of seed_events.sql.
do $$
declare n int;
begin
  select count(*) into n from clubs;
  if n <> 320 then
    raise exception 'expected 320 clubs, loaded %', n;
  end if;
end $$;
